/var/home/charlie/.hermes/webui/sessions/781a8599e120.json:1374:      "reasoning": "I have a strong updated picture. Let’s consolidate what’s currently supported versus still assumed.\n\nConfidence tier:\n- Strong evidence / direct checks:\n  - ADB reachable on NetBird and WiFi\n  - phone-network-stability: WiFi `PDCN`, NetBird `tun0`, ping to `100.87.171.39` OK, `8787/5000` reachable, Magisk keepalive running\n  - explicit root curl: LAN page at `192.168.123.71:18182/` returns HTML in 0.02s\n  - global proxy is `127.0.0.1:7890`; mihomo is running and `7890/7891/7892/5354` are listening\n  - Brave is the current foreground browser\n- Mixed/partial evidence:\n  - I have NOT validated Brave’s own page rendering for the blocked page\n  - I do not yet have an explicit `/proc/net/route`/socket-level proof that the local HTTP 502 path is the same failure seen in the browser\n  - I haven’t yet isolated whether the browser’s own HTTP stack hits the same path as my curl probes\n\nSo the current real issue is narrowed to local IPv4 HTTP page reachability under the user/browser path, not a global phone network failure. I should recommend the smallest decisive next check: verify Brave’s current page content/URL, or add one precise in-device HTTP probe that matches the browser failure more directly.用户说“我一加手机网络有问题 请检查”，当前已经收集了很多诊断信息。现有证据显示：Brave 浏览器当前前台页面是 `192.168.123.71:18182/`；Brave UID `10627` 访问这个 LAN 页面成功，但访问 DuckDNS/Google 失败；手机全局代理是 `127.0.0.1:7890`，且 mihomo 在跑；手机侧 WiFi 已连 `PDCN`，NetBird 也正常。关键异常看起来集中在浏览器出网路径，不是手机整体断网。\n\n我需要先整合现有结论，判断是 Brave 代理/DNS/页面卡住，还是全局网络问题。再补少量定向验证后，直接给结论和修复建议。",
/var/home/charlie/.hermes/webui/sessions/781a8599e120.json:1376:      "reasoning_content": "So far, the diagnosis shows:\n\n1. **Phone is on WiFi `PDCN`** with strong signal (`-33 dBm`, 104 Mbps).\n2. **NetBird is connected**, not forced relayed, Lazy=false. IP layer works fine. ping 100.87.171.39 is 21ms, 0% loss.\n3. **Phone can reach LAN services by IP**: `192.168.123.71:18182` works from Brave UID (`10627`).\n4. **Phone can reach LAN Hermes `100.87.171.39:8787` by IP from root shell** with 200 in ~0.04s.\n5. **Phone can reach internet by IP when bypassing DNS**: `http://223.5.5.5` returns 200. But HTTPS names like `https://www.google.com/generate_204` fail with `OPENSSL_internal:invalid library` from root shell when using direct HTTPS, which is a known TLS library conflict on this device. However, `su 10627 -c curl https://www.google.com/generate_204` fails with `Could not resolve host`, which suggests Brave/Browser UID path has DNS issues.\n6. **DuckDNS to Hermes `:8787` fails with 000** (connection refused after 0.737s) while LAN IP works.\n7. **Global HTTP proxy is set to `127.0.0.1:7890`**.\n8. **mihomo is running** and listening on `7890/7891/7892/5354`.\n9. **Phone-side `latest.json` is stale** and shows all failures.\n10. **`settings get global http_proxy` returns `127.0.0.1:7890`**, but that doesn't mean the system/Chrome core respects it on this device/Android version; on many modern Androids, the legacy global proxy is ignored by Chrome/Brave unless there's a dedicated VPN/proxy app or Android AutoProxy is used.\n11. **Chrome/Brave on this device likely ignores the global `http_proxy` setting**. The modern Chromium on Android often uses the Android Network Stack, but some OEM ROMs + Chromium versions ignore `Settings.Global.HTTP_PROXY`. The presence of `com.celzero.bravedns` suggests DNS is being handled separately, and Brave likely uses its own proxy settings or the system VPN stack.\n12. **DuckDNS Hermes 8787 is not reachable from the phone**, indicating that either DNS resolution for DuckDNS is failing or routing/DNAT isn't working from phone to router/WAN.\n\nI need to narrow down DuckDNS first. Earlier we saw `charlie1990.duckdns.org:8787` returned 000 from the phone, while `192.168.123.71:18182` is reachable from Brave. That means DNS might be fine (since DuckDNS resolved to an IP), but the WAN path from phone 5G to DuckDNS isn't. However, the user didn't specify whether they're on WiFi or 5G. The current state is WiFi, but the user might be experiencing issues when switching or when on 5G.\n\nI should check DuckDNS IP from the phone via DNS lookup, and compare with host WAN IP. Also check whether the phone can reach DuckDNS on port 80 (public web) to see if it's a WAN issue or Hermes-specific.\n\nI should also check whether the user's actual problem is specific: browser can't open Hermes? Or general network? The user said \"我一加手机网络有问题 请检查\", which is very vague. So the deliverable should be a clear status: what works, what doesn't, and the most likely fix.\n\nKey finding so far: **Brave browser on this device likely doesn't honor the legacy Android global HTTP proxy setting.** Evidence: `curl` from root shell with explicit proxy `-x http://127.0.0.1:7890` to `charlie1990.duckdns.org:8787` times out, but root shell direct to LAN IP `192.168.123.71:18182` works. Also, `su 10627` (Brave UID) to `192.168.123.71:18182` returns 200, but DNS names in HTTPS fail with `Could not resolve host` from that UID. This suggests Brave's network stack is not using mihomo DNS (5354) or system DNS.\n\nWait, earlier `su 10627` to `https://www.google.com/generate_204` gave `Could not resolve host`. That's DNS failure for that UID, not a network block. That's a strong hint: **Brave is not using the correct DNS path**. It might be using its own DoH or IPv6-only DNS, or not honoring the iptables DNS redirect for that UID.\n\nLet me verify DNS specifically for Brave UID vs root.\n\nI'll test DNS resolution via `nslookup` or `getent` isn't available, but I can test `curl http://(ip-of-google):80` or `curl -v http://www.google.com` to see if it resolves. Or use `ping` to an IP vs hostname.\n\nActually, I can test:\n- `su 10627 -c 'curl -sS -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code} %{time_total}s\\n\" --max-time 10 http://142.250.1.100/'` (Google IP) to see if IP works.\n- `su 10627 -c 'curl -sS -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code} %{time_total}s\\n\" --max-time 10 http://www.google.com'` to see if name resolution works.\n\nAlso test DuckDNS resolution from phone:\n- `su -c 'curl -sS http://charlie1990.duckdns.org:80/'` from root to see if DNS resolves and port 80 is reachable.\n- Check DuckDNS IP from host side.\n\nAlso, the user's actual \"network problem\" might be \"Hermes not opening in browser on phone\". Since current session is from WebUI, they might be using the browser on the same phone to access Hermes.\n\nGiven the evidence, I think the main issues are:\n1. **Brave ignores global proxy** -> LAN IP pages might work, but public/Hermes names might not route through mihomo.\n2. **DNS path for Brave is broken** -> can't resolve names when not using explicit proxy DNS.\n3. **DuckDNS -> Fedora 8787 is unreachable from phone** -> either DuckDNS doesn't resolve from phone, or WAN path is blocked.\n\nLet's get decisive evidence on DuckDNS from phone and DNS differences between root and Brave.",
/var/home/charlie/.hermes/webui/sessions/781a8599e120.json:1405:            "arguments": "{\"command\": \"adb -s 100.87.37.3:5555 shell \\\"su -c 'curl -sS -o /dev/null -w \\\\\\\"root_duckdns80=%{http_code} %{time_total}s\\\\\\\\nroot_duckdns8787=%{http_code} %{time_total}s\\\\\\\\nroot_lan=%{http_code} %{time_total}s\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\" --max-time 10 http://charlie1990.duckdns.org http://charlie1990.duckdns.org:8787/api/sessions http://192.168.123.71:18182/'\\\"\", \"timeout\": 30, \"workdir\": \"/var/home/charlie/workspace\"}"
/var/home/charlie/.hermes/webui/sessions/781a8599e120.json:1444:      "content": "{\"output\": \"curl: (7) Failed to connect to charlie1990.duckdns.org port 80 after 7069 ms: Could not connect to server\\ncurl: (7) Failed to connect to charlie1990.duckdns.org port 8787 after 8043 ms: Could not connect to server\\nroot_duckdns80=000 7.069162s\\nroot_duckdns8787=000 7.069162s\\nroot_lan=000 7.069162s\\nroot_duckdns80=000 8.043805s\\nroot_duckdns8787=000 8.043805s\\nroot_lan=000 8.043805s\\n<!DOCTYPE html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n    <meta charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\">\\n    <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\\\">\\n    <title>Android Power Tools</title>\\n    <link rel=\\\"icon\\\" type=\\\"image/png\\\" href=\\\"favicon.png\\\">\\n    <link rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\" href=\\\"bundle.css\\\">\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n    <script src=\\\"bundle.js\\\"></script>\\n    <script src=\\\"redroid-wsfix.js?v=20260809-1\\\"></script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\nroot_duckdns80=200 0.014043s\\nroot_duckdns8787=200 0.014043s\\nroot_lan=200 0.014043s\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"error\": null}",
/var/home/charlie/.hermes/webui/sessions/781a8599e120.json:1463:      "reasoning_content": "I have a strong updated picture. Let’s consolidate what’s currently supported versus still assumed.\n\nConfidence tier:\n- Strong evidence / direct checks:\n  - ADB reachable on NetBird and WiFi\n  - phone-network-stability: WiFi `PDCN`, NetBird `tun0`, ping to `100.87.171.39` OK, `8787/5000` reachable, Magisk keepalive running\n  - explicit root curl: LAN page at `192.168.123.71:18182/` returns HTML in 0.02s\n  - global proxy is `127.0.0.1:7890`; mihomo is running and `7890/7891/7892/5354` are listening\n  - Brave is the current foreground browser\n- Mixed/partial evidence:\n  - I have NOT validated Brave’s own page rendering for the blocked page\n  - I do not yet have an explicit `/proc/net/route`/socket-level proof that the local HTTP 502 path is the same failure seen in the browser\n  - I haven’t yet isolated whether the browser’s own HTTP stack hits the same path as my curl probes\n\nSo the current real issue is narrowed to local IPv4 HTTP page reachability under the user/browser path, not a global phone network failure. I should recommend the smallest decisive next check: verify Brave’s current page content/URL, or add one precise in-device HTTP probe that matches the browser failure more directly.",
/var/home/charlie/.hermes/webui/sessions/781a8599e120.json:1752:      "content": "先给你当前可确认的结论，不等补充我也继续往下做。\n\n**结果**\n- 我这边的直接结论：**手机目前是“部分通路异常”，不是完全断网。**\n- **NetBird、WiFi 局域网、本地 Hermes 都是通的**；但 **DuckDNS 公网域名目前不可达**。\n- 另外，手机走 **Brave 浏览器 UID 的访问存在间歇性异常**：有时域名解析失败，有时整条通路 timeout。\n\n**What I did**\n- 先确认 ADB 可用设备：`100.87.37.3:5555`、`192.168.123.22:5555` 都在线。\n- 跑了手机侧综合稳定性脚本：`tun0` 存在、NetBird ping 正常、`8787/5000` 可达、Magisk keepalive 模块正常。\n- 对比了多种访问路径：\n  - `100.87.171.39:8787` 可达\n  - `192.168.123.71:18182/` 在 Brave UID 下多次可达\n  - `charlie1990.duckdns.org:8787` 不可达\n- 查了手机 WiFi/NetBird 状态：\n  - 当前 WiFi：`PDCN`，`192.168.123.22`\n  - NetBird：`wt0/tun0` 正常\n  - NetBird 配置：`LazyConnectionEnabled=false`，`ForceRelayed=false`\n- 查了代理/DNS：\n  - 全局 HTTP 代理是 `127.0.0.1:7890`\n  - mihomo 在监听 `7890/7891/7892/5354`\n  - 但 Brave UID 下会出现 `Could not resolve host: www.google.com`，说明不是单纯代理端口问题\n- 查了公网 DNS 漂移：\n  - WAN IP：`103.121.208.125`\n  - DuckDNS 解析：`125.110.209.185`\n  - 两边不一致，说明 **DuckDNS 当前漂移了**\n\n**Evidence**\n- 手机稳定性脚本关键输出：\n  - `tun0` OK\n  - `ping 100.87.171.39` 平均约 `21.579ms`\n  - `8787/5000` 可达\n- 手机侧直连：\n  - `curl http://192.168.123.71:18182/` 在 Brave UID 下返回 `200`\n- 公网域名：\n  - `curl http://charlie1990.duckdns.org:8787/api/sessions` 手机侧失败\n  - `dig +short charlie1990.duckdns.org` 为 `125.110.209.185`\n  - `curl https://ipinfo.io/ip` 主机侧为 `103.121.208.125`\n- 浏览器侧异常证据：\n  - Brave UID 下部分请求返回 `000` / `Could not resolve host`\n  - 但同设备另一轮对 `192.168.123.71:18182/` 又是 `200`\n- `latest.json` 过时：\n  - `latest.json` 里还是旧状态/旧 FastIP，不能代表当前真实网络\n\n**Next step**\n- 我现在建议直接处理两个最高置信问题：\n  1. **更新 DuckDNS 记录，纠正域名漂移**\n  2. **继续补齐 Brave 浏览器实际访问页面/URL 的样本**，区分是“特定网站问题”还是“浏览器/DNS 策略问题”\n- 你如果现在能告诉我**具体是哪个页面/哪个场景卡**，我可以立刻把诊断收窄到那个路径。",
/var/home/charlie/.hermes/webui/sessions/781a8599e120.json:1954:      "content": "{\"output\": \"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# wan-ip-monitor.sh — WAN IP 变更检测 + DuckDNS 一致性 + 服务探活自愈\\n# 每60秒运行，IP不变时也检查 DNS 解析和关键端口可达性\\n# 永久化: state 存 ~/.local/state/wan-ip-monitor/\\nset -euo pipefail\\n\\nSTATE_DIR=\\\"$HOME/.local/state/wan-ip-monitor\\\"\\nIP_FILE=\\\"$STATE_DIR/last-ip\\\"\\nLOG_PREFIX=\\\"[wan-ip]\\\"\\n\\n# 配置要探活的服务（域名:端口）\\nCHECK_ENDPOINTS=(\\n  \\\"charlie1990.duckdns.org:8648\\\"\\n)\\n\\n# 加载 credentials\\nsource \\\"$HOME/.local/share/credentials/duckdns.env\\\"\\n\\nlog() { echo \\\"$LOG_PREFIX $(date '+%H:%M:%S') $*\\\"; }\\n\\n# 获取路由器真实 WAN IP。Fedora 的默认出口可能经过代理/VPN，不能用其\\n# 外部出口地址更新 DuckDNS。\\ncurrent_ip=\\\"\\\"\\ncurrent_ip=$(\\n  sshpass -p admin ssh \\\\\\n    -o BatchMode=no \\\\\\n    -o ConnectTimeout=5 \\\\\\n    -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no \\\\\\n    admin@192.168.123.1 \\\\\\n    '/usr/sbin/nvram get wan0_ipaddr' 2>/dev/null || true\\n)\\n\\nif ! [[ \\\"$current_ip\\\" =~ ^([0-9]{1,3}\\\\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}$ ]] || [ \\\"$current_ip\\\" = \\\"0.0.0.0\\\" ]; then\\n  current_ip=\\\"\\\"\\n  for i in 1 2 3; do\\n    current_ip=$(curl -4 -s --noproxy '*' --connect-timeout 5 ifconfig.me 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"\\\")\\n    [ -n \\\"$current_ip\\\" ] && break\\n    [ \\\"$i\\\" -lt 3 ] && sleep 5\\n  done\\nfi\\n\\nif [ -z \\\"$current_ip\\\" ]; then\\n  log \\\"无法获取WAN IP\\\"\\n  exit 1\\nfi\\n\\n# 读取上一次IP\\nlast_ip=$(cat \\\"$IP_FILE\\\" 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"\\\")\\n\\nheal_dns() {\\n  log \\\"DuckDNS 解析漂移: DNS=$1, current=$current_ip，强制更新\\\"\\n  result=$(curl -4 -sL --noproxy '*' \\\\\\n    --get 'https://www.duckdns.org/update' \\\\\\n    --data-urlencode \\\"domains=${DUCKDNS_DOMAIN}\\\" \\\\\\n    --data-urlencode \\\"token=${DUCKDNS_TOKEN}\\\" \\\\\\n    --data-urlencode \\\"ip=${current_ip}\\\" 2>/dev/null)\\n  if [ \\\"$result\\\" = \\\"OK\\\" ]; then\\n    log \\\"DuckDNS 自愈更新成功: $current_ip\\\"\\n    notify-send -u normal \\\"DuckDNS 自愈\\\" \\\"域名已强制更新为 $current_ip\\\" 2>/dev/null || true\\n    # 更新后再探活一次\\n    sleep 2\\n    if check_endpoint \\\"${DUCKDNS_FQDN}:8648\\\"; then\\n      log \\\"探活验证通过\\\"\\n      return 0\\n    else\\n      log \\\"探活验证仍失败，可能需要等待 DNS 生效\\\"\\n      return 1\\n    fi\\n  else\\n    log \\\"DuckDNS 自愈更新失败: $result\\\"\\n    return 1\\n  fi\\n}\\n\\ncheck_endpoint() {\\n  local ep=$1\\n  local host=${ep%%:*}\\n  local port=${ep##*:}\\n  # 先检查端口是否开放\\n  if ! curl -4 -s --noproxy '*' --connect-timeout 5 \\\"http://${host}:${port}/\\\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\\n    log \\\"探活失败: $ep\\\"\\n    return 1\\n  fi\\n  return 0\\n}\\n\\n# IP未变，检查 DuckDNS 解析一致性 + 端口探活\\nif [ \\\"$current_ip\\\" = \\\"$last_ip\\\" ]; then\\n  dns_ip=$(dig +short +timeout=3 +tries=1 \\\"${DUCKDNS_FQDN}\\\" @8.8.8.8 2>/dev/null | grep -E '^[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+$' | head -n 1 || true)\\n\\n  # 先看端口是否可达\\n  endpoint_failed=0\\n  for ep in \\\"${CHECK_ENDPOINTS[@]}\\\"; do\\n    if ! check_endpoint \\\"$ep\\\"; then\\n      endpoint_failed=1\\n    fi\\n  done\\n\\n  # 端口失败且 DNS 漂移 -> 修复\\n  if [ \\\"$endpoint_failed\\\" -eq 1 ]; then\\n    if [[ \\\"$dns_ip\\\" =~ ^([0-9]{1,3}\\\\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}$ ]] && [ \\\"$dns_ip\\\" != \\\"$current_ip\\\" ]; then\\n      heal_dns \\\"$dns_ip\\\"\\n      exit $?\\n    else\\n      log \\\"端口不可达，但 DNS=$dns_ip 与 current=$current_ip 一致，不判定为 DNS 问题\\\"\\n    fi\\n  fi\\n\\n  # 端口可达但 DNS 漂移 -> 也修复（防患未然）\\n  if [ \\\"$endpoint_failed\\\" -eq 0 ]; then\\n    if [[ \\\"$dns_ip\\\" =~ ^([0-9]{1,3}\\\\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}$ ]] && [ \\\"$dns_ip\\\" != \\\"$current_ip\\\" ]; then\\n      heal_dns \\\"$dns_ip\\\"\\n      exit $?\\n    fi\\n  fi\\n\\n  exit 0\\nfi\\n\\n# IP变更！触发DuckDNS更新\\nlog \\\"WAN IP 变更: ${last_ip:-无} → $current_ip\\\"\\n\\nresult=$(curl -4 -sL --noproxy '*' \\\\\\n  --get 'https://www.duckdns.org/update' \\\\\\n  --data-urlencode \\\"domains=${DUCKDNS_DOMAIN}\\\" \\\\\\n  --data-urlencode \\\"token=${DUCKDNS_TOKEN}\\\" \\\\\\n  --data-urlencode \\\"ip=${current_ip}\\\" 2>/dev/null)\\n\\nif [ \\\"$result\\\" = \\\"OK\\\" ]; then\\n  echo \\\"$current_ip\\\" > \\\"$IP_FILE\\\"\\n  log \\\"DuckDNS 已更新为 $current_ip\\\"\\n  notify-send -u normal \\\"WAN IP 变更\\\" \\\"$current_ip — DuckDNS 已更新\\\" 2>/dev/null || true\\n  # 更新后验证\\n  sleep 2\\n  for ep in \\\"${CHECK_ENDPOINTS[@]}\\\"; do\\n    if ! check_endpoint \\\"$ep\\\"; then\\n      log \\\"更新后探活仍失败: $ep\\\"\\n    fi\\n  done\\nelse\\n  log \\\"DuckDNS 更新失败: $result\\\"\\n  exit 1\\nfi\\n---\\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\\nset -euo pipefail\\n\\nSTATE_DIR=\\\"$HOME/.local/state/duckdns-full-monitor\\\"\\nLOG=\\\"$STATE_DIR/latest.log\\\"\\nmkdir -p \\\"$STATE_DIR\\\"\\n\\nDUCKDNS_HOST=\\\"charlie1990.duckdns.org\\\"\\nDUCKDNS_ENV=\\\"$HOME/.local/share/credentials/duckdns.env\\\"\\nsource \\\"$DUCKDNS_ENV\\\"\\n\\n# DuckDNS public port -> local port\\ndeclare -A PORT_MAP=(\\n  [18080]=8080\\n  [18094]=5000\\n  [18300]=8787\\n  [19867]=2586\\n  [19888]=19888\\n  [19899]=19000\\n  [19900]=19001\\n  [19902]=19002\\n  [19903]=19003\\n  [19904]=19004\\n  [19905]=19005\\n  [19906]=19006\\n  [19907]=19007\\n  [19976]=18999\\n  [8648]=8648\\n)\\n\\nROUTER=\\\"admin@192.168.123.1\\\"\\nROUTER_PASS=\\\"admin\\\"\\nnow() { date '+%F %T'; }\\nlog() { echo \\\"$(now) $*\\\" >> \\\"$LOG\\\"; }\\ncheck_tcp() { curl -4 -sS --noproxy '*' --connect-timeout 4 \\\"http://${1}:${2}/\\\" >/dev/null 2>&1; }\\ncurrent_ip() {\\n  local ip\\n  ip=$(sshpass -p \\\"$ROUTER_PASS\\\" ssh -o BatchMode=no -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no \\\"$ROUTER\\\" '/usr/sbin/nvram get wan0_ipaddr' 2>/dev/null || true)\\n  if [[ \\\"$ip\\\" =~ ^([0-9]{1,3}\\\\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}$ ]] && [ \\\"$ip\\\" != \\\"0.0.0.0\\\" ]; then echo \\\"$ip\\\"; return; fi\\n  curl -4 -s --noproxy '*' --connect-timeout 5 ifconfig.me 2>/dev/null || true\\n}\\ndns_ip() { dig +short +timeout=3 +tries=1 \\\"$DUCKDNS_HOST\\\" @\\\"$1\\\" 2>/dev/null | grep -E '^[0-9]+\\\\.' | head -n 1 || true; }\\nupdate_duckdns() { curl -4 -sL --noproxy '*' --get 'https://www.duckdns.org/update' --data-urlencode \\\"domains=${DUCKDNS_DOMAIN}\\\" --data-urlencode \\\"token=${DUCKDNS_TOKEN}\\\" --data-urlencode \\\"ip=${1}\\\" 2>/dev/null || true; }\\nrouter_dnat_for_port() { sshpass -p \\\"$ROUTER_PASS\\\" ssh -o BatchMode=no -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no \\\"$ROUTER\\\" \\\"iptables -t nat -L vserver --line-numbers -n | grep -E \\\\\\\"dpt:${1} \\\\\\\" | head -n 1\\\" 2>/dev/null || true; }\\nlocal_ip() { ip -4 addr show \\\"${1:-wlp0s20f0u5}\\\" 2>/dev/null | grep -oP 'inet \\\\K[0-9.]+' | head -n 1 || true; }\\n\\nlog \\\"===== run start =====\\\"\\nlog \\\"router=$(ip -4 route show default | head -n 1)\\\"\\nlog \\\"local_ip=$(local_ip wlp0s20f0u5)\\\"\\n\\ncurrent=$(current_ip)\\nlog \\\"current_ip=$current\\\"\\n\\ndns_any_fail=0\\nfor r in 8.8.8.8 223.5.5.5 1.1.1.1 119.29.29.29; do\\n  d=$(dns_ip \\\"$r\\\") || true\\n  log \\\"dns@$r=$d\\\"\\n  if [ -n \\\"$d\\\" ] && [ \\\"$d\\\" != \\\"$current\\\" ]; then dns_any_fail=1; fi\\ndone\\n\\nif [ \\\"$dns_any_fail\\\" -eq 1 ]; then\\n  log \\\"dns_drift=1 forcing update to $current\\\"\\n  update_duckdns \\\"$current\\\" | while read -r line; do log \\\"duckdns_update=$line\\\"; done\\n  sleep 2\\nfi\\n\\npublic_fail=0\\ndeclare -A FAILED_PORTS\\nfor port in $(echo \\\"${!PORT_MAP[@]}\\\" | tr ' ' '\\\\n' | sort -n); do\\n  local_port=\\\"${PORT_MAP[$port]}\\\"\\n  local_ok=0; public_ok=0\\n  check_tcp \\\"127.0.0.1\\\" \\\"$local_port\\\" && local_ok=1 || true\\n  check_tcp \\\"$DUCKDNS_HOST\\\" \\\"$port\\\" && public_ok=1 || true\\n  log \\\"port=$port local=$local_ok public=$public_ok\\\"\\n  if [ \\\"$local_ok\\\" -eq 1 ] && [ \\\"$public_ok\\\" -eq 0 ]; then\\n    public_fail=1\\n    FAILED_PORTS[$port]=1\\n    rule=$(router_dnat_for_port \\\"$port\\\") || true\\n    log \\\"port=$port public_fail rule=${rule:-none}\\\"\\n  fi\\ndone\\n\\nfrpc_ok=0; frps_ok=0\\nsystemctl --user is-active --quiet frpc.service 2>/dev/null && frpc